From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: PreviewKeyDown/Up, TextCommandBarFlyout, Popup name scope, ListView selection, deferred compiled elements

NanaZip's address bar wires itself in its OnApplyTemplate and stopped at the first part we did not have, so Enter in the box did nothing. Now: TextCommandBarFlyout and CommandBarFlyout are made (placement, primary and secondary commands, Opened/Closed/Opening kept; shown when popups are), and a TextBox exposes its later interfaces (ITextBox4-8: selection and context flyouts accepted); PreviewKeyDown and PreviewKeyUp tunnel from the root down to the focused element before KeyDown/KeyUp route up, a handler setting Handled stopping both and the box's own use of the key; FindName and GetTemplateChild find a Popup's child (its name scope); ListView keeps a selection (SelectionMode, SelectedIndex, SelectedItem, IsItemClickEnabled); a ScrollViewer shows its content even when an implicit style gives it a template naming parts we do not make yet (ScrollContentPresenter, scroll bars); compiled markup's deferred elements of newer compilers (section reference kind 9: x:Load, x:DeferLoadStrategy) are left unrealized instead of failing the template. With these NanaZip takes a path typed into its address bar and goes there. Interface identity per windows-rs 0.30.0 (MIT); kind 9's layout from observed files; the implementation is ours. Behind the XAML switch of 6131.
---
